   "why": [
    "Tub width 18->11 cm gives ~16 cm overall (+<=1.0 cm steering error) well inside 19.8 cm. Battery 4.8->14.4 Wh (6 cells: 2 in pack + 4 on hand, free) gives 12.2 Wh usable against ~6 Wh needed for 5 km even with +108 g (energy/m ~4.2 J/m). Both are within the current parts' ranges, so no swap is needed.",
    "The bump switch has no parameters, so no params move can help. The HC-SR04 ranges 2 m in any light, so the robot can run at cruise speed through the dark corridor: 11 m at ~0.6-0.9 m/s is ~15-20 s. It adds no height and only 0.08 W. Camera only lights 0.12 m in the dark (< body length); lidar is not provided."
